# The exception panel 172's critic measured in its own fifty lines
# (2026-09-21): a Heroes panic while a lease is live reached the same SIGABRT
# handler and printed a second, false line saying a C function freed the lease.
# Panel 173 judged the fix; this golden pins that a runtime-initiated abort
# says one thing, the true one, and nothing about C.

extern "a-panic-with-a-live-lease-says-one-thing.h"
    function look(s: cstr lent)

function main()
    x = "payload"
    c: cstr @ x.lease()
    look(s: c)
    a = [1, 2, 3]
    print(to_str(a[9]))
    end_lease(@c)
